      "message": "tation of the upstream semantics: `float(value) / 100.0` (cents \u2192 dollars).\n- **`_load_producer()`** \u2014 loads `committed/A_direct/producer.py` by file path via `importlib.util.spec_from_file_location`, returning `None` if the file is missing, unloadable, lacks `normalize_price`, or reports a different `CONTRACT_VERSION`.\n- **`normalize_price(value)`** \u2014 delegates to the producer function when loaded, otherwise falls back to the copied implementation.\n- **`consume(value)`** \u2014 the requested downstream entry point; returns `normalize_price(value)`, i.e. the price converted from minor units (cents) to major units (dollars).\n- **`__main__` block** \u2014 asserts `consume(1234) == 12.34`, `consume(0) == 0.0`, `consume(100) == 1.0`, and parity between the delegated and copied paths.\n\nThe contract assumption carried transitively (version 1, `normalize_price(value) -> float(value) / 100.0`) is documented in the module docstring so the artifact remains correct even if the upstream file is unavailable."
